    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Tai kingdom founded in 1228 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukaphaa">Sukaphaa</a> that ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> for six centuries.</li><li>The paik system made every free adult man owe labour or military service, supporting roads, embankments and armies.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahom-people">Ahoms</a> resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, winning at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saraighat">Saraighat</a> in 1671, before rebellion and Burmese invasions ended the state.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Ahom kings were buried in earthen mounds called maidams at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charaideo">Charaideo</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO</a> inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 2024.</p></aside>
    </section>

